Types, Variables, Fundamentals
ASCII • No Borders • Copyable

====================================================================
TYPE DEFINITIONS
====================================================================

TYPE SID = {Structure, Interaction, Dynamics}
TYPE PED = {Power, Evaluation, Dynamics}

TYPE RDG_Operator =
    IsoOp          // metric‑preserving map
    PhaseOp        // angle/phase extraction
    AlignOp        // micro‑alignment (Δ‑resolution)
    SimOp          // similarity/proportional operator
    LinMap         // homothety / linear scaling
    ConicDyn       // constrained‑motion curve generator
    MomentEq       // equilibrium solver
    ProjExtract    // projective direction extractor

TYPE Instrument =
    VernierCaliper
    DividerCompass
    Protractor
    Sector
    ProportionalDivider
    Ellipsograph
    BalanceScale
    SurveyQuadrant


====================================================================
VARIABLES
====================================================================

r_main        // main scale reading
r_vernier     // vernier scale reading
k             // coincidence index
d(P,Q)        // metric distance between points P and Q
θ             // angular phase variable
a,b           // ellipse semi‑axes parameters
x(θ), y(θ)    // parametric curve coordinates
m1, m2        // masses on balance arms
d1, d2        // moment arms
dir(P)        // projective direction of point P
λ             // linear scaling factor (homothety)
Δ             // micro‑alignment offset


====================================================================
RDGMFEQ FUNDAMENTALS
====================================================================

FUNDAMENTAL_RELATIONAL_PRIMITIVES:
    Metric(P,Q)
    Angle(P,Q,R)
    Direction(P)
    Constraint(Motion)
    Equilibrium(Interaction)
    Similarity(Relation)
    Scaling(Relation)
    ConicState(Motion)

FUNDAMENTAL_MFE_COMPONENTS:
    PED.Power      // constraint or force source
    PED.Evaluation // extracted relational state
    PED.Dynamics   // motion or settling behavior


====================================================================
INSTRUMENT → RDGMFEQ OPERATOR MAPPINGS
====================================================================

--------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Vernier Calipers → AlignOp (SID.Interaction)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
RDG:
    AlignOp(r_main, r_vernier) =
        min_k | r_main - r_vernier + k*ε |

PED:
    Power      = sliding constraint
    Evaluation = coincidence index k
    Dynamics   = micro‑alignment process

--------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Dividers & Compasses → IsoOp (SID.Structure)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
RDG:
    IsoOp(P,Q,P',Q') : d(P,Q) = d(P',Q')

PED:
    Power      = fixed radius constraint
    Evaluation = metric equality
    Dynamics   = rotational sweep

--------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Protractor → PhaseOp (SID.Evaluation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
RDG:
    PhaseOp(P,Q,R) = θ = angle(P,Q,R)

PED:
    Power      = geometric projection
    Evaluation = phase θ
    Dynamics   = static readout

--------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Sector → SimOp (SID.Structure + Interaction)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
RDG:
    SimOp(a,b,c,d) : a/b = c/d

PED:
    Power      = hinge angle defines similarity class
    Evaluation = transversal intercept
    Dynamics   = leg sliding

--------------------------------------------------------------------
5. Proportional Divider → LinMap (SID.Structure)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
RDG:
    LinMap(x) = λ * x

PED:
    Power      = fixed mechanical ratio λ
    Evaluation = scaled distance
    Dynamics   = rigid linkage

--------------------------------------------------------------------
6. Ellipsograph / Trammel → ConicDyn (SID.Dynamics)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
RDG:
    x(θ) = a*cos(θ)
    y(θ) = b*sin(θ)

PED:
    Power      = orthogonal slot constraints
    Evaluation = parametric state θ
    Dynamics   = continuous constrained motion

--------------------------------------------------------------------
7. Balance / Scale → MomentEq (SID.Interaction)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
RDG:
    MomentEq(m1,m2,d1,d2) : m1*d1 = m2*d2

PED:
    Power      = gravitational potential
    Evaluation = equilibrium condition
    Dynamics   = pivot settling

--------------------------------------------------------------------
8. Surveying Quadrant → ProjExtract (SID.Structure)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
RDG:
    ProjExtract(P) = dir(P)

PED:
    Power      = line‑of‑sight constraint
    Evaluation = projective angle
    Dynamics   = static alignment


====================================================================
RDGMFEQ SYNTHESIS
====================================================================

SID.Structure:
    IsoOp, LinMap, ProjExtract

SID.Interaction:
    AlignOp, SimOp, MomentEq

SID.Dynamics:
    ConicDyn

PED.Power:
    constraints, forces, radii, hinges

PED.Evaluation:
    angles, distances, ratios, equilibrium states

PED.Dynamics:
    motion‑generated curves, settling equilibria


====================================================================
SUMMARY
====================================================================

This ASCII block encodes the RDGMFEQ interpretation of:
    • classical drafting instruments
    • surveying tools
    • curve‑generating mechanisms
    • proportional calculators
as relational geometric operators in the SID/PED dual‑triad framework.
